---
import { ArrowLeft } from "lucide-react";
import StatusDashboard from "../dashboard";
import { MAIN_WEBSITE } from "../site-links";
import "../styles.css";

const links = [
  { name: "Main site", href: MAIN_WEBSITE },
  { name: "Reports", href: `${MAIN_WEBSITE}/reports` },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0c0a09" />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
    <meta name="description" content="Rail Radar API reachability, provider health, and 30-day response times from real station requests and scheduled checks." />
    <title>Rail Radar status</title>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/Geist-web.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/GeistMono-core.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#providers">Skip to providers</a>
    <main class="site-width">
      <a class="back-link" href={MAIN_WEBSITE}><ArrowLeft aria-hidden="true" />Back to Rail Radar</a>
      <div class="page-intro">
        <h1>Rail Radar status</h1>
        <p>Our API and the data providers behind your next departure.</p>
      </div>
      <StatusDashboard client:load />
      <noscript><p class="no-script">Enable JavaScript to load current status and explore provider history.</p></noscript>
      <section class="methodology" aria-label="About these observations">
        <div><h2>Real requests, plus regular checks</h2><p>Recorded when visitors request station boards, and every hour Rail Radar requests departures at each provider's busiest station. Cached responses add no observations.</p></div>
        <div><h2>As fresh as traffic allows</h2><p>Provider health needs at least 5 observations. It uses the last hour when there are enough, otherwise the last 3 or 24 hours. Errors and timeouts are failures: 5% is degraded, 50% is a major disruption.</p></div>
        <div><h2>Latency, without the guesswork</h2><p>Daily p50, p90 and p99 over 30 UTC days. Missing timings stay empty. Today is partial; tail percentiles need larger samples.</p></div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="site-width footer-inner">
        <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Rail Radar status"><span class="status-mark"><img src="/favicon.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span><span>Rail Radar <span class="brand-section">Status</span></span></a>
        <span class="footer-tagline">NO TICKET REQUIRED.</span>
        <nav aria-label="More from Rail Radar">{links.map((link) => <a href={link.href}>{link.name}</a>)}</nav>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
